captain jack sparrow may be the  protagonist of the pirates of the  caribbean movies but he's definitely no  hero cannibal capers dastardly double  crossings and the creepiest seduction in  the franchise these are the most  terrible things jack sparrow has ever  done  the daughter of the fearsome pirate  blackbeard angelica forsook her father's  life of piracy clung to her catholic  faith and decided to become a nun  instead before taking her vows however  angelica is seduced by a young jack  sparrow who whisks her away from the  nunnery and leads her into a life of  crime after their time together  frustrated by a string of betrayals  angelica is left heartbroken by jack but  she has no way back to her old life  either because of this she eventually  joins her father's quest to find the  fountain of youth which jack also  manages to ruin by contributing to the  death of blackbeard himself at the  film's end rather than apologizing for  his mistakes or even just taking her  back to civilization jack strands  angelica on a deserted island ruining  her life yet again  jack sparrow and betrayals go together  like ships and the sea no matter who you  are your relation to him or how aligned  you think your goals might be jack will  always find a way to twist the scenario  to his own benefit at your expense  in curse of the black pearl jack  convinces commodore james norrington to  engage with captain barbosa and his men  on the isla de muerta in a surprise  attack only to immediately reveal said  plan to barbosa in exchange for his own  life  roberts your uncle fanny's your aunt  there you are with two ships  this results in the slaughter of many of  norrington's men as barbossa's skeleton  army takes them out one by one nearly  overtaking their ship  much of the blood spilled during this  attack is directly the result of jack's  meddling but it is later revealed to be  part of his master plan soon after jack  and will turner lift the skeletal curse  and barbosa's army are returned to their  normal human forms just in time for the  british to overtake the pirates sparing  the rest of their lives  this little stunt still cost the lives  of countless men however and it's fair  to say that jack really doesn't seem all  that cut up about it  if dead man's chest taught us anything  about jack it's that he's definitely not  an innocent man  both earthly authorities and  supernatural beings have pursued him  across the caribbean  after meeting back up with will turner  jack sends the boy off to the flying  dutchman to join davy jones's crew in an  effort to save his own skin  he has no problem telling jones that  will soul should count towards his own  mystical debt  of course nothing is quite that simple  in the pirates universe  jones demands more souls than just will  but he's happy to take the young pirate  nonetheless so jack happily leaves will  to his fate heads to tortuga and tries  to collect 99 more souls innocent people  who will be condemned to servitude so  that jack can escape a promise he once  made it's not exactly his finest hour  earlier in dead man's chest will find  jack and his crew run aground on a  tribal island somewhere in the caribbean  on this island jack was somehow able to  become the tribe's leader but what he  doesn't know is that the members of the  tribe have planned to eat him he  eventually escapes although he seems to  be fully aware that the tribe has been  saving will and his crew for the fleshly  feast  when will meets up with jack rather than  telling will to free the crew and help  them get out of there he begs will to  save him alone with no consideration for  the crew at all now sure jack was as  much a prisoner of the cannibal tribe as  anyone but when jack and the crew first  arrived on the island he probably could  have convinced the locals not to lock up  his friends  knowing jack's inherent selfishness it's  clear he was only thinking of himself  and if will hadn't arrived there's no  telling what would have happened to the  crew  after being resurrected in at world's  end jack quickly makes a deal with lord  cutler beckett the governor of the east  india trading company beckett wants  information about the brethren court the  pirate lords and the nine pieces of  eight jack does him one better he tells  beckett that he'll lead him to shipwreck  cove the meeting place of the pirate  lords then at shipwreck cove jack plans  to convince the pirates to go to war so  that they can be annihilated by beckett  and his vast armada why would jack do  this well his original end game was to  flee ship wreck cove and sail the seas  forever as the last of his kind  quite like the sound of that  captain jack sparrow  the last pirate  and so jack makes his deal with beckett  and leads him to the meeting place of  the pirates then true to his word he  convinces them to sail out and fight  while jack sparrow clearly works in  mysterious ways and beckett is  eventually defeated it's easy to imagine  that jack's plan to betray his fellow  swashbucklers was genuine even just for  a little while  a recurring thread throughout the  original pirates of the caribbean  trilogy is that jack has a bit of a  crush on elizabeth swann unfortunately  for jack elizabeth is strong confident  and fearless meaning she's really not  the type of girl who would be interested  in him knowing full well how will feels  about her however jack constantly  attempts to take advantage of and seduce  elizabeth including by getting her drunk  on a beach naturally elizabeth is a bit  too smart for jack and she manages to  use her feminine prowess against him at  the end of dead man's chest by the time  jack sees elizabeth again he doesn't  seem to trust her but eventually comes  around and supports her as the new  pirate king when the chips are down  still his constant pursuit of elizabeth  earlier in the series provides an  unsettling glimpse into jack's  womanizing ways  check out one of our newest 